.TH lc "" "Command"
.SH NAME
lc \- categorize files in a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlc [\-1abcdfmp] [\fIdirectory ...\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
lc -- categorize files in a directory
Usage:	lc [ -1abcdfp ] [ directory ... ]
Options:
	-1	List files one per line instead of in columns
	-a	List all files in directory (including '.' and '..')
	-b	List block special files only
	-c	List character special files only
	-d	List directories only
	-f	List regular files only
	-p	List pipe files only
The options can be combined.
If there is no 'directory' specified, the current directory is used.
.HE
.B lc
lists the files in each named
.IR directory ,
or in the current directory if none is named.
Unless one of
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-c\fR, \fB\-d\fR, \fB\-f\fR, \fB\-m\fR, or \fB\-p\fR
restricts the listing to one type, all six types are listed, each
under its own heading (``Directories'', ``Files'', ``Character
special files'', ``Block special files'', ``Pipes'', ``Multiplexed
files''), sorted by name and packed into columns that fit the
terminal width.
When more than one
.I directory
is given, each is preceded by its own name.
.IP \fB\-1\fR
List one file name per line instead of packing them into columns.
.IP \fB\-a\fR
Include
.B .
and
.B ..
in the listing.
.IP \fB\-b\fR
List block-special files only.
.IP \fB\-c\fR
List character-special files only.
.IP \fB\-d\fR
List directories only.
.IP \fB\-f\fR
List regular files only.
.IP \fB\-m\fR
List multiplexed (multiplexor) files only.
This option is accepted by the program but is not mentioned in its
built-in usage message or in the Options table above.
.IP \fB\-p\fR
List pipe files only.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B ls
.SH NOTES
.B "lc -f"
is useful for producing a list of regular file names, for example to
feed to another command via command substitution.
